{:edb/db-before-t 2214 :edb/db-after-t 2215 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535527 50 #inst "2026-10-09T01:50:06.991Z" 13194139535527 true] [17592186171892 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353698 13194139535527 true] [17592186171892 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353713 13194139535527 true] [17592186171952 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353691 13194139535527 true] [17592186171952 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353705 13194139535527 true] [17592186171952 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353720 13194139535527 true] [17592186353691 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353692 13194139535527 true] [17592186353691 1089 "q-115836" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353691 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535527 true] [17592186353691 1100 "Solve the inequality $\\frac{2x+5}{({x}^{2}+3)(2-x)}>0.$" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353691 1113 #uuid "12ec4938-eb26-5d97-a9e5-0e654fa11c89" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353691 1145 "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2x+5}{({x}^{2}+3)(2-x)}.\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)>0.$\n\nThe solution to the equation $f(x)=0$ is $x=-\\frac{5}{2}.$ Also, $f(x)$ has vertical asymptote at $x=2.$  The root and the asymptote divide the number line into $3$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{2}),\\,(-\\frac{5}{2},2),\\,(2,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{2})$ | $(-\\frac{5}{2},2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2x+5$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| ${x}^{2}+3$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $2-x$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)>0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive in the interval $(-\\frac{5}{2},2).$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (-\\frac{5}{2},2).$" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353693 13194139535527 true] [17592186353692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353694 13194139535527 true] [17592186353692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353695 13194139535527 true] [17592186353692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353696 13194139535527 true] [17592186353692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353697 13194139535527 true] [17592186353692 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535527 true] [17592186353692 1041 "selection" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353692 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353693 13194139535527 true] [17592186353692 1110 #uuid "7bd3ec06-fb08-5207-a992-08a33da51ed7" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353693 1034 "x\\in (-\\frac{5}{2},2)" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353693 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353693 1111 #uuid "447c54fa-843c-555a-a73c-b8697bb862d8" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353694 1034 "x\\in (-\\frac{5}{2},\\infty )" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353694 1111 #uuid "4172aa23-ca1c-5cf4-9548-e5e14b9e6e5b" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353695 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{2})\\cup (2,\\infty )" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353695 1111 #uuid "51325632-f660-5384-a161-cdc54cda055f" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353696 1034 "x\\in (2,\\infty )" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353696 1111 #uuid "6d7a3c2d-ae5b-5d8c-98c3-8d74e2f07cdb" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353697 1034 "x\\in (-\\frac{5}{2},-2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353697 1111 #uuid "fc14a16b-48f3-52df-9e64-bf329dea3118" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353698 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353699 13194139535527 true] [17592186353698 1089 "q-115978" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353698 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535527 true] [17592186353698 1100 "Solve the inequality $\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-5x}<0.$" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353698 1113 #uuid "ab49cabc-074b-5c94-8d39-a16e173ce902" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353698 1145 "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-5x}.\n$$\n\nBy factoring its denominator, the function $f(x)$ can be rewritten as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2}{x(x-5)}.\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)<0.$\n\nThe function $f(x)=0$ has no solution. On the other hand, $f(x)$ has vertical asymptotes at $x=0$ and $x=5.$ These asymptotes divide the number line into $3$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,0),\\,(0,5),\\,(5,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $(0,5)$ | $(5,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-5$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)<0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the interval $(0,5).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (0,5).$" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353700 13194139535527 true] [17592186353699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353701 13194139535527 true] [17592186353699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353702 13194139535527 true] [17592186353699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353703 13194139535527 true] [17592186353699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353704 13194139535527 true] [17592186353699 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535527 true] [17592186353699 1041 "selection" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353699 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353704 13194139535527 true] [17592186353699 1110 #uuid "5ad0de1d-f54f-5372-aceb-bd35325bc8ec" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353700 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-5)\\cup (0,5)" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353700 1111 #uuid "afcc0710-03b0-59a6-8454-cc02b92b035b" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353701 1034 "x\\in (0,\\infty )" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353701 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353701 1111 #uuid "29260512-10cb-5e52-829c-dcf37317766b" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353702 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (5,\\infty )" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353702 1111 #uuid "4981a775-126d-5c53-925a-82fd163b6b64" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353703 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,5)" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353703 1111 #uuid "2958ddfe-2360-58bf-a816-b61bf0230450" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353704 1034 "x\\in (0,5)" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353704 1111 #uuid "83bd6d6a-1f8d-5139-93d7-1f4f53b617f0" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353705 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353706 13194139535527 true] [17592186353705 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353709 13194139535527 true] [17592186353705 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353711 13194139535527 true] [17592186353705 1089 "q-324342" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353705 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535527 true] [17592186353705 1100 "The values of $x$ that satisfy the inequality  $\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{x+1}\\ge 0$ lie in the interval\n\n$\\,x\\in [$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)⋃[$\n{{field-3}}$,\\infty ).$" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353705 1113 #uuid "8bcd6c69-554f-5b0a-95f0-12381ca7ad79" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353705 1145 "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-5$ and $x=2.$ Also, $f(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x=-1.$ The roots and asymptote divide the number line into $4$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-5),\\,(-5,-1),\\,(-1,2),\\,(2,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-5)$ | $(-5,-1)$ | $(-1,2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+5$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-2$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x+1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the intervals $(-5,-1)$ and $(2,\\infty ).$ Since the function equals zero at $x=-5$ and at $x=2,$ we include these endpoints in the solution.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nf(x)\\ge 0\\,\\text{for all}\\,x\\in [\\,-5,-1\\,)⋃[\\,2,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353707 13194139535527 true] [17592186353706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353708 13194139535527 true] [17592186353706 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535527 true] [17592186353706 1041 "field-1" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353706 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353707 13194139535527 true] [17592186353706 1110 #uuid "4b417f02-47a0-543a-b504-73b3606d4037" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353707 1034 "-5" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353707 1111 #uuid "513bfde9-209d-55d3-a6c1-d14b536b27b2" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353708 1034 "5" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353708 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353708 1111 #uuid "84645be2-e821-5be0-9ad5-03dd678f64f8" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353710 13194139535527 true] [17592186353709 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535527 true] [17592186353709 1041 "field-2" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353709 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353710 13194139535527 true] [17592186353709 1110 #uuid "ec8b8fbf-ce1b-5c5a-9f7c-bc0d6baf5792" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353710 1034 "-1" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353710 1111 #uuid "802765bd-721d-5468-b027-cdd97a48c156" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353711 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353712 13194139535527 true] [17592186353711 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535527 true] [17592186353711 1041 "field-3" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353711 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353712 13194139535527 true] [17592186353711 1110 #uuid "309d386d-1d2a-53ec-9216-5931fd233ebf" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353712 1034 "2" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353712 1111 #uuid "2d10e739-cb17-5dc8-b70b-1c5ef4b5b6bd" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353713 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353714 13194139535527 true] [17592186353713 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353716 13194139535527 true] [17592186353713 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353718 13194139535527 true] [17592186353713 1089 "q-326139" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353713 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535527 true] [17592186353713 1100 "The values of $x$ that satisfy the inequality $\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+15}{x+2}\\ge 0$ lie in the interval\n\n$\\,x\\in [$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$]⋃($\n{{field-3}}$,\\infty ).$" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353713 1113 #uuid "ff8c41fd-4007-5e0e-bd90-44213e7e6540" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353713 1145 "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+15}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nBy factoring its numerator and denominator, the function $f(x)$ can be rewritten as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{(x+3)(x+5)}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-5$ and $x=-3.$ Also, $f(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x=-2.$ The roots and asymptote divide the number line into $4$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-5),\\,(-5,-3),\\,(-3,-2),\\,(-2,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-5)$ | $(-5,-3)$ | $(-3,-2)$ | $(-2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x+5$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x+2$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the intervals $[-5,-3]$ and $(-2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, remembering that the roots of $f(x)$ are also solutions, we conclude that \n\n$$\nf(x)\\ge 0\\,\\text{for all}\\,x\\in [-5,-3\\,]\\cup (-2,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353715 13194139535527 true] [17592186353714 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535527 true] [17592186353714 1041 "field-1" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353714 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353715 13194139535527 true] [17592186353714 1110 #uuid "48058ad1-56a4-57b8-b249-71edecc1f204" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353715 1034 "-5" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353715 1111 #uuid "892b0bcb-f0d2-51ce-b4af-050e7fadfce7" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353717 13194139535527 true] [17592186353716 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535527 true] [17592186353716 1041 "field-2" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353716 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353717 13194139535527 true] [17592186353716 1110 #uuid "fad23a4d-afdd-5836-bb20-dbc43002af85" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353717 1034 "-3" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535527 true] [17592186353717 1111 #uuid "35a0eada-63a2-5faf-9e19-5a92a2458c97" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353719 13194139535527 true] [17592186353718 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535527 true] [17592186353718 1041 "field-3" 13194139535527 true] [17592186353718 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353719 13194139535527 true] [1